/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 54 0 R
/E (Comparing DNA and protein sequences is an important task in bioinformatics for identifying similarities, mutations, conserved regions, and evolutionary relationships. Traditional sequence comparison methods may not effectively identify highly similar regions within larger sequences, especially when mutations, insertions, or deletions are present.)
